{'user': [{'id': 1, 'text': 'I think I need to go to accident and emergency'}, {'id': 2, 'text': 'my neck is stiff and I am in a lot of pain'}], 'bot': [{'id': 1, 'text': "I'm sorry to hear that. It's important to seek medical attention if you have a severe injury or symptoms that concern you. Accident and emergency (A&E) departments are equipped to handle urgent and life-threatening situations. Please go to your nearest A&E or call for emergency services if you believe your condition is critical. Don't hesitate to seek help; your health is a priority.", 'score': 50}, {'id': 2, 'text': "A stiff neck can be caused by minor sprains and strains, which can be caused by sleeping in an awkward position, sitting or slouching for long periods, repeatedly looking down at objects like a cell phone, or sustaining a sports injury.

