Did you mean to ask about dysarthria?', 'score': 50}, {'id': 5, 'text': "The long-term symptoms of COVID-19 can include depression, anxiety, and fatigue. A study by Taquet's team showed that 47% of the 475 people who were hospitalised with COVID-19 and discharged before 31 March 2021 had moderate to severe depression at the second assessment compared with 34% at six months, 40% had moderate to severe fatigue compared with 26% in the first tests, and the proportion of people with moderate to severe anxiety rose from 23% to 27%. The results of the cognitive assessments were unchanged, with an average cognitive deficit equivalent to 10 IQ points at both initial and follow-up tests.", 'score': 50}]}

