{'user': [{'id': 1, 'text': 'I am 35 weeks pregnant my chest hurts when breathing and I feel lightheaded'}, {'id': 2, 'text': 'What kind of medical advice'}], 'bot': [{'id': 1, 'text': "In the later stages of pregnancy, some chest discomfort is to be expected. If you're lying on your back, you might also experience a shortness of breath, sweating and lightheadedness. This is because your uterus is compressing the vena cava and aorta. To relieve this, it is recommended that you sleep on your left side.

However, it is important to note that ongoing dizziness or lightheadedness could be a sign of more serious health issues such as preeclampsia, a stroke, a heart or lung problem, bleeding or problems with blood sugar levels. If you have any concerns, it is always best to seek medical advice.", 'score': 50}, {'id': 2, 'text': "Medical advice is the provision of a formal professional opinion regarding what a specific individual should or should not do to restore or preserve health. Typically, medical advice involves giving a diagnosis and/or prescribing a treatment for a medical condition. Medical advice can be distinguished from medical information, which is the relation of facts. Discussing facts and information is considered a fundamental free speech right and is not considered medical advice. Medical advice can also be distinguished from personal advice, even if the advice concerns medical care.

