{'user': [{'id': 1, 'text': 'I am pregnant and am experiencing a pain in my chest and breathlessness'}, {'id': 2, 'text': 'I have swelling in my left leg as well and redness'}, {'id': 3, 'text': 'What about swelling and redness in one leg during pregnancy'}], 'bot': [{'id': 1, 'text': "You should see your doctor immediately if you have chest pain that doesn’t go away, is severe, or if you have other symptoms that happen even when you’re resting or lying down. It's also important to get urgent medical attention if you have severe shortness of breath or difficulty breathing, sudden breathlessness, chest pain that worsens when coughing, excessive nausea and vomiting, dark urine or peeing less than usual, leg or ankle swelling, leg or ankle swelling on one side only, swelling of the face or anywhere in your body, or calf muscle pain or leg pain.

